      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T19:12:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know.\n\n* I see that `SkWuffsCodec::frame` (which is called by another override of `SkFrameHolder::onGetFrame`) only returns `nullptr`.\n* OTOH, I see that `SkWebpCodec::FrameHolder::frame` only `SkASSERT`s that the index is valid.\n* FWIW transitive callers of `SkFrameHolder::onGetFrame` either `SkASSERT` that they got non-null, or just start dereferencing it...\n* Here `SkPngRustCodec` works a bit [similarily to `SkWuffsCodec::onGetFrameInfo`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkWuffsCodec.cpp;l\u003d861-864;drc\u003d04989307509c78d67b34f2282ca549397719d046) in that the our `getFrameInfo` implementation also assumes that out-of-bounds index will return `nullptr`.  I note that `onGetFrameInfo` is an internal API, but it may be [called](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/include/codec/SkCodec.h;l\u003d744;drc\u003d04989307509c78d67b34f2282ca549397719d046) from the public `getFrameInfo` API without fully validated index.\n\nI think we can just continue returning null (mostly because of the last point).",
